@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

#
# prima-materia — the rule against reporting the absence, examined
#
# The statement at pmc:TheRuleAgainstReportingTheAbsence named two falsifiers:
# that its witnesses are not of one kind, and, more cheaply, a count, if rules
# of this shape stood in only a small minority of the transmissions that make a
# promise. It stood at the head of queries/untested-generalizations.rq with
# seven witnesses. This protocol makes the count against the whole holding and
# reads every candidate the count turned up.
#

pmp:RuleAgainstReportingTheAbsenceExamination a pm:Testing ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the rule against reporting a failure is a device of operative transmissions or a handful of cases"@en, "Ob die Regel gegen das Melden eines Fehlschlags ein Mittel operativer Überlieferungen ist oder eine Handvoll Fälle"@de ;
    skos:definition "A protocol on the claim that a recurring device in operative transmissions attaches a consequence to the practitioner's report that the result did not come, in three forms: the saying causes the failure, the saying is an offence, the saying is evidence about the speaker. The population is every tradition in the holding that stands beyond pm:corpusNamed, 107 on 2026-10-17 on main, and within it the 75 that carry at least one pm:Yielding or pm:Attributing, that is, a promise of a capacity. Drawn by a whole-graph scan of the labels, definitions and notes of every node with pm:withinTradition for doubt, disbelief, unbelief, complain, no benefit, of no use, not cured, tell anyone, faith, faithless, scoff, mock and blame, which returned hits in 74 traditions; every node a hit fell on whose label or wording suggested a rule about failure or doubt was read at the node."@en ;
    pm:tests pmc:TheRuleAgainstReportingTheAbsence ;
    pm:falsifiedBy "First, as the statement names it: the witnesses are not of one kind, each being a rule against disclosing the method or against public complaint in general rather than against the report that the result failed to come. Not met. Second, also as the statement names it: rules of this shape stand in a small minority of the transmissions that make a checkable promise. Met in the plain sense of the words: eight of 107 entered transmissions, five of the 75 that carry a coded promise."@en ;
    pm:examinationState pm:casesWithDeviation ;
    pm:baseRate "Eight traditions of the 107 in the holding beyond pm:corpusNamed carry the device as a rule stated in the material, about one in thirteen; five of the 75 traditions that carry a pm:Yielding or pm:Attributing node, one in fifteen. Three of the eight carry no such node, so the second figure undercounts the device by the coding of promises and not by the material."@en ;
    pm:counterSearch pm:counterSearchFoundOpposition ;
    pm:counterSearchNote "Searched: the compiled holding as of 2026-10-17 on main, by the scan in the definition. Read at the node, besides the seven witnesses: pmc:AgrippaCulpaLectoris, pmc:RasarnavaNastikasyaAsiddhi, pmc:TurbaCulpaInOperante, pmc:CmBuxindaoDispute, pmc:LeDouteAffaiblitLaPuissance, pmc:CautionAgainstWitnesses, pmc:QuimbyAmiciIncreduli, pmc:NebesnyiListNeverie, pmc:JainaLingamNaTrayate, pmc:ChanKounianXinbuxing, pmc:FraudKnownAndBeliefHeld, pmc:SwedenborgSignaNonCoguntFidem, pmc:SubidaDeumNonInterrogandum, pmc:RomanusProbaAdIncredulum, pmc:NkasaVerdictRule, pmc:VaidikaDosavivadah, pmc:GehongDaoyiBuji, pmc:TiantaiFeiMoSuoWei. Found for the statement: one witness of the third form not yet counted, Agrippa. Found against it: the proportion, and the four opposite cases the statement already names, of which none is overturned. Not searched: the works themselves; the count is a count of what harvesters wrote down, and a rule of this kind in an opened work that the harvest passed over is not in it."@en ;
    pm:examinedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-17" ;
    pm:protocolUpdated "2026-10-17" ;
    skos:note "The first falsifier holds off, and the protocol adds one witness of the kind the statement names. Agrippa closes De occulta philosophia with a rule on the saying itself: whoever through incredulity or dulness does not obtain his desire is not to say that the author erred or wrote falsely and lied, but is to accuse himself (pmc:AgrippaCulpaLectoris). The forbidden utterance is named and it is the report of a failure; the speaker's incredulity is the account given of it. That is the third form, in print, from a learned author outside any lineage. The node was already a witness of the statement about where a failed run is put, and it now stands under both, which is the stacking the statement's own note describes."@en ;
    skos:note "What the scan found next to the device and does not count, and the line between them, since it is the line a wider reading would cross. Seven transmissions attach the failure to a doubt or an unbelief held before or during the operation and not to a report after it: the magnetiser whose doubt of his own power enfeebles it (pmc:LeDouteAffaiblitLaPuissance), the incredulous spectator who troubles the somnambulist (pmc:CautionAgainstWitnesses), the Jain ascetic filled with deceit (pmc:JainaLingamNaTrayate), the Chan reciter whose mind does not practise (pmc:ChanKounianXinbuxing), the Russian heavenly letter that curses whoever does not believe it (pmc:NebesnyiListNeverie), the faith rule reported by a hostile chronicler of the Celestial Masters (pmc:CmBuxindaoDispute), the Quimby patients who hold their faith against sceptical friends (pmc:QuimbyAmiciIncreduli). They fall under the statement about where a failed run is put, or under none. Two further nodes are true cases of the device and stand in traditions already counted: the Rasārṇava verse that denies accomplishment to whoever says it does not exist (pmc:RasarnavaNastikasyaAsiddhi), the first form, and the Turba's blame not the Wise but yourselves (pmc:TurbaCulpaInOperante), which forbids the same accusation of the author that Agrippa forbids, the third form. They raise the count of witnesses and not of traditions."@en ;
    skos:note "The second falsifier is met, and the protocol does not argue it away. The statement worded its claim as a recurrence and not a proportion, and in the same node named a small minority as the condition under which it should be withdrawn to a remark about its cases. Eight of 107 is a small minority in any ordinary sense. What the count also shows is that the eight are not a cluster: China twice, a Kongo corpus, an Indian alchemical work, a Latin alchemical dialogue, a Hebrew ascent text, a modern German esoteric course and a printed Renaissance handbook, in at least six languages, from the fourth century to the twentieth, with only the two Chinese cases of one period and region. A device that recurs at that spread and that rate is neither a rule of the material nor a handful of cases, and the statement is rewritten at the node to say both: a recurring minority device, with the rate."@en ;
    skos:note "Why the rate is a lower bound and how much lower is unknown. The statement's own note gave the reason before the count was made: where the device works, adherents do not report failures, and nothing records the rule unless it is written down. The count adds a second reason that belongs to this holding: it counts what harvesters wrote, and many of the 107 traditions stand on one or two works read in part. A protocol that wanted the rate in the material rather than in the holding would draw a sample of fully harvested works and read each for the rule; on 2026-10-17 the holding marks one tradition as pm:corpusHarvested and one as pm:workOpened, which is too few to draw from."@en ;
    skos:note "A case from the run of the same day stands on a branch not yet merged and is recorded here so that it is not lost: the Hindi commentator of the Gorakṣapaddhati says at the term of a year that one is not to doubt whether accomplishment comes, and in his preface that the unbelievers who call the accomplished frauds do so because they do not practise, and that if they practised, accomplishment would become visible. The second is the third form applied to an outsider's saying and not to a practitioner's report, the near edge the statement's note already marks at the Zande case. It is not counted."@en ;
    skos:note "The cheapest next question is the denominator. A pm:corpusHarvested tradition read whole for the rule, and found without it, would be the first case in which the absence of the device is attested rather than inferred from the holding, and it is what would turn the lower bound into a rate."@en .
